<!-- ===== FAQs ===== -->
<section class=\"faq-section\" style=\"margin:48px 0;\">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions About PPC Management in Dubai</h2>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>What is the minimum budget for Google Ads in Dubai?</h3>
<p>There is no technical minimum — Google Ads can technically run on any budget. However, in Dubai\'s competitive market, we generally recommend a <strong>minimum monthly ad spend of AED 3,000–5,000</strong> to gather sufficient data for optimisation and see meaningful results. For highly competitive sectors like real estate or finance, AED 10,000–30,000+/month is more appropriate. Our <a href=\"/contact/\">free PPC audit</a> will give you a tailored budget recommendation for your specific industry and goals.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>What ROAS (Return on Ad Spend) should I expect?</h3>
<p>Well-managed Google Ads accounts in the UAE typically achieve <strong>ROAS of 4:1 to 8:1</strong> for e-commerce, meaning AED 4–8 in revenue for every AED 1 spent. Service businesses typically measure success differently — through cost-per-lead rather than direct revenue ROAS. During campaign setup, we agree on realistic KPI benchmarks based on your industry benchmarks and historical account data. Check our <a href=\"/case-studies/\">case studies</a> for real UAE client results.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>How long does it take to set up a Google Ads campaign?</h3>
<p>Our standard onboarding process takes <strong>7–14 business days</strong> from kick-off to live campaigns. This includes account audit (if inheriting existing campaigns), keyword research, audience segmentation, ad copywriting, conversion tracking setup, landing page review, and campaign build. For clients needing faster launches, we offer an expedited 5-day setup for straightforward campaign structures.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>Which advertising platforms do you manage?</h3>
<p>We manage campaigns across all major platforms relevant to UAE advertisers: <strong>Google Ads</strong> (Search, Display, Shopping, YouTube, Performance Max), <strong>Meta Ads</strong> (Facebook and Instagram), <strong>LinkedIn Ads</strong> (ideal for B2B and professional services), <strong>Snapchat Ads</strong> (highly effective for the UAE\'s young demographic), <strong>TikTok Ads</strong>, and <strong>Microsoft Advertising</strong>. Platform recommendations are driven by your audience profile and objectives, not by what\'s easiest for us to manage. Explore our <a href=\"/services/social-media-marketing/\">social media marketing</a> service for complementary organic and paid social strategies.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>How do you report on campaign performance?</h3>
<p>Every client receives a <strong>monthly performance report</strong> covering impressions, clicks, CTR, conversions, cost-per-conversion, ROAS, Quality Scores, and budget utilisation. Reports are delivered via dedicated dashboards with real-time data access — you\'re never waiting for a monthly PDF to understand what\'s happening with your budget. We also conduct monthly strategy calls to review performance and agree on the following month\'s optimisation priorities.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>Do you charge a management fee on top of ad spend?</h3>
<p>Yes — our management fee is separate from your advertising spend, which goes directly to Google/Meta/LinkedIn. We offer two fee structures: a <strong>flat monthly management fee</strong> (predictable costs, suitable for established accounts) or a <strong>percentage of ad spend</strong> model (scales with your investment, suitable for growing accounts). Both structures are discussed transparently before any agreement is signed.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>Can you take over an existing Google Ads account?</h3>
<p>Yes — account takeovers are a common starting point. We\'ll conduct a comprehensive audit of your existing account, identify waste, document historical performance baselines, and implement a phased improvement plan. Inherited accounts often show 20–40% efficiency gains within the first 90 days through negative keyword cleanup, Quality Score improvement, and restructuring poorly organised campaign architecture.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>What makes Dubai PPC different from other markets?</h3>
<p>Several factors make UAE PPC uniquely complex: <strong>multilingual targeting</strong> (Arabic and English audiences behave very differently), <strong>elevated CPC rates</strong> (the highest in MENA), <strong>diverse expat demographics</strong> requiring nuanced audience segmentation, <strong>cultural sensitivity</strong> in ad creative, and <strong>platform usage patterns</strong> that differ from Western markets (e.g., WhatsApp click-to-chat ads are highly effective in UAE). Local expertise isn\'t a nice-to-have — it\'s a competitive necessity. Visit our <a href=\"/dubai/\">Dubai digital marketing page</a> for market-specific insights.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>How do you handle Arabic language PPC campaigns?</h3>
<p>Arabic PPC campaigns require more than translating English ads. We develop native Arabic ad copy crafted for search intent, ensure keyword matching accounts for Arabic morphology (root-based language structure means many variations of a single concept), and create Arabic-language landing pages that match ad messaging. Our team includes Arabic-speaking digital strategists with deep knowledge of UAE consumer behaviour.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>What is Quality Score and why does it matter?</h3>
<p>Quality Score is Google\'s 1–10 rating of your ad\'s relevance based on three factors: <strong>expected click-through rate, ad relevance to the keyword, and landing page experience</strong>. A higher Quality Score directly reduces your cost-per-click — a QS of 8 can mean paying 50% less per click than a competitor with QS of 4 for the same keyword. Our optimisation process systematically improves Quality Scores across all campaigns, reducing costs while maintaining or improving reach.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>Do you run remarketing campaigns?</h3>
<p>Yes — remarketing is a core part of our PPC strategy for all clients. We build remarketing audiences segmented by behaviour (e.g., viewed product page, abandoned cart, visited pricing page), and serve tailored ads that speak to where each visitor is in their buying journey. UAE remarketing campaigns consistently deliver <strong>3x higher ROAS</strong> than cold prospecting, making them one of the highest-leverage PPC tactics available.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>Can PPC work for B2B companies in Dubai?</h3>
<p>Absolutely. B2B PPC in Dubai is particularly effective on <strong>LinkedIn Ads</strong> (targeting by industry, job title, company size, and seniority), <strong>Google Search</strong> (capturing high-intent procurement searches), and <strong>remarketing</strong> (maintaining visibility through the longer B2B buying cycle). We\'ve run successful B2B campaigns for consultancies, technology firms, manufacturing companies, and professional services providers across the UAE. See our <a href=\"/blog/\">blog</a> for B2B PPC strategy insights.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>What happens if my campaigns aren\'t performing?</h3>
<p>Underperformance triggers an immediate diagnostic review: we analyse search term reports, Quality Scores, conversion path data, audience segments, and competitor activity to identify root causes. We communicate findings to clients transparently and implement a structured improvement plan. No campaign performs optimally from day one — iterative optimisation over the first 60–90 days is a normal part of every engagement.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"border-bottom:1px solid #e0e0e0;padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>Should I run PPC and SEO at the same time?</h3>
<p>Yes — this is our recommended approach for most businesses. PPC generates immediate leads while <a href=\"/services/search-engine-optimization/\">SEO</a> builds long-term organic authority. PPC data (which keywords convert, which audiences engage, what messaging resonates) directly informs and accelerates your SEO strategy. Over time, strong organic rankings reduce your reliance on paid spend, improving overall marketing ROI. Our integrated approach ensures both channels reinforce each other. <a href=\"/contact/\">Talk to us about a combined strategy</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class=\"faq-item\" style=\"padding:20px 0;\">
<h3>How do I get started with PPC management in Dubai?</h3>
<p>Start with our <strong>free PPC audit</strong>. Whether you\'re starting from scratch or have an existing account, we\'ll review your situation, benchmark against industry performance, identify key opportunities and inefficiencies, and provide a clear roadmap. There\'s no obligation to proceed — we want you to make an informed decision. <a href=\"/contact/\">Book your free PPC audit today</a>.</p>
</div>

</section>

