<h2>Frequently Asked Questions: Web Development in Dubai</h2>

<h3>How long does web development take for a Dubai business website?</h3>
<p>Development timelines vary by project complexity. A straightforward business website on WordPress typically takes 3–6 weeks for development once designs are approved. WooCommerce e-commerce stores generally require 6–12 weeks. Custom web applications with complex back-end logic and integrations typically take 12–24 weeks or more. The development timeline runs concurrently with or follows the <a href=\"/services/web-design/\">web design</a> phase, so total project timelines from kick-off to launch are typically 8–24 weeks depending on scope. We provide a detailed timeline in every project proposal.</p>

<h3>What CMS options do you recommend for UAE businesses?</h3>
<p>WordPress is our primary recommendation for most business websites — it powers 43% of the internet for good reason. It has the most mature ecosystem of plugins, themes, and developer support globally, and it\'s the platform your team can most easily learn to manage. For e-commerce, WooCommerce (built on WordPress) is our default recommendation, with Shopify considered for simpler product catalogues. For enterprise projects requiring custom content architectures, we sometimes use WordPress as a headless CMS with a Next.js front-end. We recommend against platform builders like Wix and Squarespace for any business serious about SEO and long-term scalability.</p>

<h3>Where will my website be hosted?</h3>
<p>We recommend and configure managed hosting environments appropriate to the project scale. For most business websites, managed WordPress hosting providers (WP Engine, Kinsta, or Cloudways) offer the best balance of performance, security, and cost. For enterprise projects or applications requiring more control, we configure AWS EC2 or DigitalOcean droplets. All our hosting recommendations include UAE or Middle East data centre options for PDPL compliance and regional performance. We do not lock clients into any specific hosting provider — the hosting account is always in the client\'s name.</p>

<h3>How do you handle website security?</h3>
<p>Security is integrated throughout our development process. We follow OWASP Top 10 security guidelines, implement SSL certificates, configure Web Application Firewalls, set up automated malware scanning, harden file permissions, implement strong authentication controls, and conduct security testing before every launch. For WordPress specifically, we lock down admin access, disable file editing, and configure a comprehensive security plugin suite. We also include security monitoring in our ongoing maintenance plans, as threats evolve continuously.</p>

<h3>Can you integrate my website with third-party systems?</h3>
<p>Yes — API and third-party integration is a core part of our development capability. We regularly integrate websites with CRM systems (HubSpot, Salesforce, Zoho CRM), email marketing platforms (Mailchimp, Klaviyo, ActiveCampaign), payment gateways (Stripe, PayTabs, Telr, HyperPay), ERP systems, inventory management platforms, booking systems, WhatsApp Business API, and custom REST APIs. We document all integrations thoroughly so your team understands the data flows and dependencies.</p>

<h3>Do you build websites that support Arabic and English?</h3>
<p>Yes. Bilingual Arabic/English development is a specialisation of ours. True Arabic RTL support goes beyond CSS — it requires rethinking layout logic, typography, form behaviour, and icon direction for the right-to-left reading context. We build bilingual sites using WordPress\'s multilingual plugins (WPML or Polylang) with proper language switching, hreflang tags for SEO, and native RTL CSS using logical properties. We test with native Arabic speakers before launch.</p>

<h3>What happens if my website breaks after launch?</h3>
<p>All clients on our monthly maintenance plans have priority support response times — typically same-day or next-business-day for non-critical issues, and within 2 hours for site-down emergencies. We maintain recent backups for rapid restoration. For clients not on a maintenance plan, we provide paid emergency support. We recommend all business websites have some form of ongoing support arrangement, as unmonitored WordPress sites can develop issues over time through plugin conflicts, WordPress updates, or security events.</p>

<h3>Can you take over maintenance of a website someone else built?</h3>
<p>Yes — we regularly take on maintenance and development of websites built by previous agencies or freelancers. We conduct a full technical audit first to assess the current state of the codebase, security, performance, and technical debt. We\'ll be honest about what we find: sometimes a site can be maintained effectively; other times a rebuild is the more cost-effective long-term solution. The audit cost is credited against any subsequent project.</p>

<h3>How do you approach accessibility and WCAG compliance?</h3>
<p>We build to WCAG 2.1 Level AA as a baseline standard for all projects. This includes sufficient colour contrast, keyboard navigability, screen reader compatibility (ARIA labels), alternative text for images, and focus indicators. For government tenders and large enterprise clients, we can provide accessibility audit reports and remediation documentation. Accessibility also improves SEO — accessible HTML is semantically correct HTML, which search engines read more effectively.</p>

<h3>Will my website perform well on Google Core Web Vitals?</h3>
<p>Yes — we target 85+ on Google PageSpeed Insights mobile score for every project. This requires performance-conscious development from the start: optimised images (WebP format, appropriate sizing, lazy loading), minimised CSS and JavaScript, efficient font loading, CDN delivery for static assets, and server-side caching. We verify Core Web Vitals compliance in both lab and field data before launch. Strong Core Web Vitals scores contribute to <a href=\"/services/search-engine-optimization/\">SEO performance</a> and provide a better experience for the 78% of UAE users on mobile devices.</p>

<h3>Do you offer e-commerce development for UAE businesses?</h3>
<p>Yes. We build WooCommerce stores integrated with UAE payment gateways (Stripe, PayTabs, Telr, HyperPay, Amazon Payment Services), UAE shipping providers, and where required, UAE customs and VAT calculation systems. We also handle complex product configurations — variable products, subscriptions, bundles, and digital downloads. For UAE e-commerce businesses, we pay particular attention to mobile checkout flow, as approximately 68% of UAE e-commerce transactions are completed on mobile devices. Learn more about our <a href=\"/services/ppc-management/\">PPC management</a> services to drive paid traffic to your e-commerce store.</p>

<h3>What is your development quality assurance process?</h3>
<p>Every project goes through a structured QA process before launch: cross-browser testing (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge), cross-device testing (iOS and Android, multiple screen sizes), functionality testing of all forms and interactive elements, performance testing, security scanning, accessibility checking, and SEO technical review. We maintain a comprehensive pre-launch checklist with over 60 checkpoints that every project must pass. We also conduct load testing for e-commerce sites and any project expecting significant traffic volumes.</p>

<h3>Can you build a custom web application — not just a website?</h3>
<p>Yes. In addition to websites, we build custom web applications: SaaS products, client portals, booking and reservation systems, directory and marketplace platforms, membership sites, and internal business tools. These projects typically use our Laravel or Node.js back-end stack with a React or Next.js front-end. We follow agile development methodology with regular sprint reviews so clients see and provide feedback on progress throughout the build — not just at the end.</p>

<h3>Do you provide the source code and documentation?</h3>
<p>Absolutely. All source code for client projects is owned by the client. We deliver projects via a version-controlled Git repository (GitHub or Bitbucket), with comprehensive technical documentation covering the system architecture, deployment procedures, third-party integrations, and CMS usage. We never retain ownership of client code or create proprietary dependencies that lock clients into working with us. Our goal is to build your capability and independence, not dependency.</p>

<h3>How do you handle website updates and WordPress version upgrades?</h3>
<p>WordPress core, theme, and plugin updates are the most common source of website issues if not managed carefully. Major WordPress updates occasionally introduce breaking changes that require developer attention. Our maintenance service manages all updates on a staging environment first, verifies compatibility and functionality, then deploys to live — never updating production directly. We also monitor the WordPress security team\'s disclosures and apply security patches as a priority outside the normal update schedule when critical vulnerabilities are announced.</p>

