<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>Which social media platform is most effective for businesses in Dubai?</h3>
<p>Depends on your business type. Instagram leads for B2C and lifestyle brands. LinkedIn dominates B2B. TikTok grows rapidly for younger demographics. Facebook still offers the broadest advertising reach across all UAE demographics.</p>

<h3>How much should a Dubai business spend on social media marketing?</h3>
<p>Most Dubai SMEs benefit from AED 5,000–15,000 per month covering content creation, community management, and paid promotion. Consistency beats volume — do fewer platforms well rather than all platforms poorly.</p>

<h3>Should UAE businesses post in Arabic or English?</h3>
<p>Ideally both. Posts including Arabic receive 45% higher engagement from UAE audiences. For cosmopolitan Dubai audiences, bilingual (Arabic + English) captions are most effective.</p>

<h3>How important is influencer marketing in the UAE?</h3>
<p>Very. 63% of UAE consumers have purchased after seeing an influencer recommendation. Micro-influencers (10K–100K followers) typically deliver higher engagement and more authentic content than mega-influencers.</p>

<h3>What content performs best on Instagram in the UAE?</h3>
<p>Reels outperform all other formats, generating 30% more non-follower reach. Video content generates 3x more engagement than static images. Cultural content (Ramadan, UAE National Day) also performs strongly.</p>

<h3>What is the best time to post on social media in the UAE?</h3>
<p>Most platforms peak 7–10pm weekday evenings. During Ramadan, post-Iftar (8–11pm) is peak time. LinkedIn exceptions: weekday mornings (7–9am) and lunch hours (12–1pm) work best for B2B content.</p>

