<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>How long does e-commerce SEO take in the UAE?</h3>
<p>Initial improvements appear within 2–3 months. Significant organic traffic growth occurs within 6–9 months, with major gains in the 12–18 month range as content and domain authority build.</p>

<h3>Should I optimise my UAE e-commerce site in Arabic?</h3>
<p>Yes. 35% of product searches in the UAE are conducted in Arabic. An Arabic-optimised store (not just a translation) can capture significant additional organic traffic with proper hreflang implementation.</p>

<h3>How do I compete with Amazon.ae and Noon for SEO?</h3>
<p>Focus on niche specialisation, content depth, and long-tail keywords where large marketplaces don\'t compete effectively. Expert niche content consistently outranks mass-market platforms for specific queries.</p>

<h3>What is the most important e-commerce SEO factor?</h3>
<p>Unique, comprehensive product and category page content delivers the highest ROI for most UAE e-commerce stores. Many sites suffer from thin content or copied manufacturer descriptions that provide no SEO value.</p>

<h3>Do product reviews help e-commerce SEO?</h3>
<p>Yes. Reviews add fresh, keyword-rich content automatically, improve dwell time, and can generate rich snippets (star ratings) that increase click-through rates by up to 35%.</p>

<h3>What is structured data and do I need it for my UAE e-commerce store?</h3>
<p>Product schema shows price, availability, and ratings in search results. It can increase click-through rates by 30–45% and is strongly recommended for all UAE e-commerce sites.</p>

<h3>How important is page speed for UAE e-commerce rankings?</h3>
<p>Very important. A 1-second improvement in mobile load time increases e-commerce conversions by 3.3%. For UAE stores where 78% of purchases begin on mobile, speed optimisation is critical.</p>

