<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>How often should I run a technical SEO audit for my UAE website?</h3>
<p>Quarterly audits are recommended for active UAE websites. Also run full audits after major redesigns, CMS migrations, or significant content restructuring. Large e-commerce sites benefit from monthly automated monitoring.</p>

<h3>What are the most critical technical SEO issues to fix first?</h3>
<p>Prioritise: (1) Indexation issues — if Google can\'t index your pages, nothing else matters. (2) Crawl errors and broken links. (3) Core Web Vitals — especially mobile speed. (4) Missing canonical tags. (5) Duplicate content.</p>

<h3>What tools are best for technical SEO auditing?</h3>
<p>Google Search Console is essential and free. Screaming Frog or Sitebulb for comprehensive crawling. Ahrefs and Semrush for cloud-based ongoing monitoring. PageSpeed Insights and Chrome DevTools for performance analysis.</p>

<h3>How important are hreflang tags for UAE websites with Arabic content?</h3>
<p>Critical. Without proper hreflang, Google may serve English pages to Arabic-speaking users and vice versa. Correct hreflang ensures the right language version reaches the right user.</p>

<h3>How long does it take to see improvements after fixing technical SEO issues?</h3>
<p>Crawl error fixes show impact within 2–4 weeks. Page speed improvements affect Core Web Vitals field data over 28 days. Major ranking improvements typically appear within 1–3 months after comprehensive fixes.</p>

