<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>How long does real estate SEO take to work in Dubai?</h3>
<p>Real estate is one of the most competitive fields in Dubai SEO, typically requiring 6–12 months for significant organic traffic growth. Early wins are achievable in 3–4 months for long-tail neighbourhood and investment keywords.</p>

<h3>Should Dubai real estate agencies focus on SEO or portal listings?</h3>
<p>Both serve different purposes. Portal listings drive immediate leads but are increasingly expensive. Your website SEO builds a long-term traffic asset you own and control. The most successful agencies invest in both.</p>

<h3>What are the most important SEO pages for a Dubai real estate website?</h3>
<p>Neighbourhood/area landing pages are the highest-value pages. Each major area needs its own comprehensive page. Off-plan project pages and buyer guide content are also high-value targets.</p>

<h3>Do Google reviews help real estate SEO in Dubai?</h3>
<p>Yes, significantly. Google reviews directly impact local map pack rankings and click-through rates. Actively request reviews from satisfied clients immediately after successful transactions.</p>

<h3>Is Arabic-language SEO important for Dubai real estate?</h3>
<p>Very. Arabic property searches represent a significant underserved market with lower competition than English equivalents — attractive for agencies willing to invest in quality Arabic content.</p>

