<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>What is a good Google Ads budget for a Dubai business?</h3>
<p>For most Dubai service businesses, a minimum of AED 8,000–12,000 per month in ad spend is needed to gather meaningful data. Highly competitive industries like legal or real estate may require AED 20,000–50,000 monthly to compete effectively.</p>

<h3>How do I measure the ROI of my Google Ads campaigns?</h3>
<p>Track ROAS for e-commerce and Cost Per Lead vs Customer Lifetime Value for service businesses. Ensure conversion tracking in both Google Ads and GA4. Connect to your CRM to track which leads actually convert to revenue.</p>

<h3>What is Quality Score and why does it matter?</h3>
<p>Quality Score (1–10) measures ad relevance, expected CTR, and landing page experience. Each 1-point improvement reduces CPC by ~13%. UAE advertisers with poor Quality Scores often overpay 50–100% vs competitors with optimised accounts.</p>

<h3>Should Dubai businesses use Arabic language Google Ads?</h3>
<p>Yes. Arabic campaigns often have 30–50% lower CPCs than English equivalents due to less competition, while reaching genuinely interested Arabic-speaking searchers. A culturally adapted Arabic campaign can deliver excellent ROI.</p>

<h3>How long does it take for Google Ads to start working in Dubai?</h3>
<p>Ads can drive traffic within 24–48 hours of launch. Campaigns need 4–8 weeks to fully optimise as Google\'s algorithm collects data. Expect month 1 to be a learning phase with improving performance from month 2 onwards.</p>

