<section class=\"mistakes\">
  <h2>Common AI Search Mistakes UAE Businesses Make</h2>
  <p>Most businesses in Dubai are aware that AI search exists but make critical strategic errors in how they respond to it. Avoiding these mistakes is as important as executing the right tactics.</p>

  <ol style=\"padding-left:20px;line-height:1.9;\">
    <li><strong>Treating AI Search as identical to traditional SEO:</strong> Keyword density and backlink counts alone do not earn AI citations. Businesses that simply apply their existing SEO playbook to AI search miss the structural and authority signals that actually determine AI citation selection.</li>
    <li><strong>Ignoring schema markup:</strong> Many UAE business websites have no structured data whatsoever. This makes them nearly invisible to AI engines that rely on schema to understand content type, authorship, and relevance.</li>
    <li><strong>Neglecting Arabic-language AI optimization:</strong> The UAE is a bilingual market. Businesses that optimize only in English miss the growing Arabic-language AI query volume, including queries from Emirati nationals and Arabic-speaking expat communities.</li>
    <li><strong>Publishing low E-E-A-T content:</strong> AI engines are trained to deprioritise anonymous, uncredentialed content. Blog posts and service pages without clear author attribution, expertise signals, and external citations are rarely cited.</li>
    <li><strong>Ignoring competitor AI citations:</strong> If your competitor is consistently cited by ChatGPT for your core service category and you aren\'t, you are losing brand consideration every single day. Regular competitive AI citation audits are essential.</li>
    <li><strong>Failing to optimise for conversational queries:</strong> AI users phrase questions differently from traditional search users. Content that targets only short-tail keywords misses the long, conversational queries that drive AI answer generation.</li>
    <li><strong>Waiting for AI search to \"mature\":</strong> Businesses that delay AI Search Optimization while waiting for the landscape to stabilise are allowing competitors to accumulate citation authority that will become increasingly difficult to displace.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

